  "final_message": "`channel` cannot be safely dropped from the [`OrderPlaced`](file:///C:/avg/w3/r/orders-service/src/core/events.ts#L7-L26) event or the [`Order`](file:///C:/avg/w3/r/orders-service/src/core/order.ts#L16-L29) model because downstream consumers still strictly depend on it.\n\n### Downstream Dependency: `analytics-ingest`\n\nWhile `channel` is not read elsewhere inside `orders-service`, checking the referenced downstream services shows that **`analytics-ingest` (team Data)** relies directly on this field:\n\n1. **Published Service Contract**: In [analytics-ingest/README.md](file:///C:/avg/w3/r/analytics-ingest/README.md#L26-L32), the contract with `orders-service` explicitly requires:\n   ```markdown\n   - `OrderPlaced`: `orderId`, `placedAt` (ISO-8601 datetime), `channel` (`web|store|marketplace`), `currency`, `lines[].sku`, `lines[].qty`\n   ```\n2. **Schema Validation**: In [`decodeOrderPlaced`](file:///C:/avg/w3/r/analytics-ingest/src/core/events.ts#L25-L46), `analytics-ingest` strictly validates incoming events:\n   ```ts\n   const channel = reader.oneOf(\"channel\", CHANNELS);\n   ```\n3. **Breaking Impact**: If `channel` is dropped from `OrderPlaced`, ingestion fails with a [`ContractViolationError`](file:///C:/avg/w3/r/analytics-ingest/src/core/errors.ts#L10-L15) (verified by tests in [`analytics-ingest/test/ingest.test.ts`](file:///C:/avg/w3/r/analytics-ingest/test/ingest.test.ts#L88-L94)), causing order data lake ingestion to reject all orders and write nothing.\n\n### Recommendation\nBefore removing `channel` from `orders-service`, team Data must first update `analytics-ingest` to make `channel` optional or deprecate its usage in the data lake pipeline.\n",
